    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required that **membership level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days**, so a brand-new owner (zero tenure) never exceeds level 3 \u2014 even one that maxes the pre-tenure factors (email + `namesakeCount` of 0 + a 3-member household).\n\nI updated `AssignMembershipLevel.java` (the step wired into `owners.POST.yml` after household/namesake counting):\n\n- **Added the household factor** so the raw level can actually reach 4: `+1` when `householdSize >= 3`. Previously the base/email/namesake factors capped at 3, which made the spec's \"is level 3, not 4\" distinction unreachable \u2014 the household point is what makes 4 possible.\n- **Gated level 4 behind tenure**: if the computed level is \u2265 4 but tenure (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now)`) is \u2264 365 days, it's capped back to 3.\n- A newly created owner's `registrationDate` defaults to the server date (`BuildOwner`), so its tenure is 0 \u2192 the cap always applies \u2192 a new owner lands at level 3, matching the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test.\n\nI also refreshed the Javadoc to describe the new factor and the tenure requirement.\n\nNote: this repo isn't a git repository, so there's nothing to commit.",
