    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change extends the existing class without distorting its shape:\n\n- The class stays single-purpose \u2014 compute and assign `membershipLevel` at creation. The new household factor is just one more increment in the same accumulate-then-cap pattern already established, so it reads naturally alongside the email and namesake factors.\n- The tenure logic is factored into a private `tenureDays(owner)` helper rather than inlined, keeping `service` readable as a linear sequence of business rules. The null-guard lives in the helper where it belongs.\n- `TENURE_DAYS_FOR_LEVEL_4` is a well-named constant rather than a bare `365`, and the cap condition (`level >= 4 && tenure <= threshold`) sits where the old `level > 3` cap was, so the \"cap at 3\" concern remains in one place rather than being scattered.\n- No duplication introduced; nothing leaks into other units. The household factor genuinely belongs here since it feeds the same level computation.\n- The expanded Javadoc matches the codebase's habit of documenting the full scoring rule on this class, and the inline comment on the cap is proportionate.\n\nNothing is in the wrong unit and no class or method is becoming a catch-all. A maintainer of this file would find the addition idiomatic.",
